      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\n\tassert(n>0);\n\tassert(s>0);\n\tassert(s<n);\n\tassert(n<8000);\n\n\t// Flat row-major storage: contiguous rows improve SIMD loads/stores.\n\tstd::vector<int> matrix((size_t)n * n);\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++) {\n\t\tint* row = &matrix[(size_t)i * n];\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++)\n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &row[j]);\n\t}\n\n\t// colSum[k] is the sum of rows [i, i+s) in column k.\n\tstd::vector<long long> colSum(n, 0);\n\tfor(int r=0;r<s;r++) {\n\t\tconst int* row = &matrix[(size_t)r * n];\n\t\t#pragma omp simd\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++)\n\t\t\tcolSum[j] += (long long)row[j];\n\t}\n\n\t// Initial SxS window sum.\n\tlong long sum = 0;\n\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\n\t\tsum += colSum[j];\n\n\tlong long mxSum = sum;\n\n\tint dir = 1;\n\tint i = 0;\n\tint j = 0;\n\twhile(i+s <= n) {\n\t\tif( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) {\n\t\t\tint exitingRow = i;\n\t\t\tint enteringRow = i+s;\n\t\t\tif(enteringRow >= n) break;\n\n\t\t\tconst int* exitPtr = &matrix[(size_t)exitingRow * n];\n\t\t\tconst int* enterPtr = &matrix[(size_t)enteringRow * n];\n\n\t\t\t// Vertical slide: update every column sum independently.\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<n;k++)\n\t\t\t\tcolSum[k] += (long long)enterPtr[k] - exitPtr[k];\n\n\t\t\t// Adjust only the columns belonging to the current window.\n\t\t\tlong long delta = 0;\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:delta)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=j;k<j+s;k++)\n\t\t\t\tdelta += (long long)enterPtr[k] - exitPtr[k];\n\t\t\tsum += delta;\n\n\t\t\ti++;\n\t\t\tdir*=-1;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tint exitingCol, enteringCol;\n\t\t\tif(dir==1) {\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = j;\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = exitingCol + s;\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = j-1;\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = enteringCol + s;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t// Horizontal slide is now O(1) using the maintained column sums.\n\t\t\tsum += colSum[enteringCol] - colSum[exitingCol];\n\t\t\tj+=dir;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif(sum > mxSum)\n\t\t\tmxSum = sum;\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Maintaining per-column sums of the current S-row band turns every horizontal slide into an O(1) add/subtract, while vertical slides update all columns with a vectorizable SIMD loop. Flat row-major storage gives contiguous accesses for NEON/GCC auto-vectorization. The serpentine traversal remains scalar, so no illegal cross-iteration dependency is introduced; long long accumulators avoid intermediate overflow while the final value still fits in 32 bits and prints identically.",
  "notes": "The algorithm preserves the exact sliding-window order of positions: horizontal moves use colSum[entering]-colSum[exiting], vertical moves update all column sums with an independent SIMD loop and adjust only the current window's columns. OpenMP SIMD pragmas are used only on loops whose iterations are truly independent or reductions, keeping all loop-carried dependencies intact.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Replace vector-of-vectors matrix with flat contiguous row-major storage for better cache and SIMD behavior",
    "Maintain a running column-sum array for the current S-row band so horizontal window slides become O(1)",
    "Update all column sums in one OpenMP SIMD loop when sliding vertically, preserving independence across columns",
    "Use long long accumulators to avoid intermediate overflow while printing the same final decimal value"
  ]
